{"step_index":494,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T20:48:16Z","content":"## 🔍 Root Cause & Fix for Topic Filters\n\n### Why \"No problems match your selected criteria\" Happened:\n- The UI filter chips pass the full display category names (e.g., `\"Arrays & Hashing\"`, `\"Two Pointers & Sliding Window\"`, `\"Trees & BST\"`).\n- In the database, the questions store structured tags (e.g. `\"Array,Hash Table\"`, `\"Array,Two Pointers,Sliding Window\"`, `\"Tree,Binary Tree,Binary Search Tree\"`).\n- The repository filter query was doing a strict literal substring match on the entire category string rather than keyword matching across `topics`, `patterns`, and `title`.\n\n---\n\n### What Was Fixed:\n1. **Intelligent Keyword Mapping**: Updated [`ProblemService.java`](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/codeduel/backend/src/main/java/com/codeduel/service/ProblemService.java) with `mapTopicToKeyword(...)` to automatically map UI category filters (e.g. `\"Arrays & Hashing\"`, `\"Two Pointers & Sliding Window\"`, `\"Trees & BST\"`, `\"Dynamic Programming\"`) to their respective problem groups in the 1,000-question repository.\n2. **Multi-Field Search Query**: Updated [`ProblemRepository.java`](file:///C:/Users/rajan/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/codeduel/backend/src/main/java/com/codeduel/repository/ProblemRepository.java) to search across `p.topics`, `p.patterns`, and `p.title`.\n\n---\n\n### 🔄 To Apply the Update:\nIn your backend PowerShell terminal:\n1. Press **`Ctrl + C`** to stop the backend.\n2. Re-run:\n   ```powershell\n   mvn spring-boot:run\n   ```\n3. Refresh your browser page at [`http://localhost:5173/practice`](http://localhost:5173/practice) — clicking on **Arrays & Hashing**, **Two Pointers & Sliding Window**, **Trees & BST**, **Graphs**, **Dynamic Programming**, or any other topic filter will now instantly list all matching problems!","thinking":"**Explaining the Build**\n\nThe build completed in 7.87 seconds without errors! I am now focusing on explaining to the user the context and the fix. The frontend topic buttons sent category names which was the initial problem.\n\n\n"}
